; Interprets: RFC 4006
;; What RFC 4006's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order. RFC 8506 obsoletes the document, and its own file reads
;; RFC 8506's text; TS 32.299 reads the credit-control AVPs from RFC 4006,
;; TS 29.212 from RFC 8506. A block with no scope, or within a grouped AVP,
;; holds wherever a document reading RFC 4006's AVP reads it; a block on
;; the CCR or CCA binds RFC 4006's own print of the command, which no other
;; document's print shares (docs/constraints.md, Precedence). The
;; credit-control session spans the CCRs and CCAs of its INITIAL_REQUEST,
;; UPDATE_REQUESTs and TERMINATION_REQUEST, so what one message carries by
;; an earlier one is `text-only`, as is what turns on the node, the
;; subscriber's account or the server's rating.


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-auth-application-id-credit-control
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 3.1
"The Auth-Application-Id MUST be set to the value 4, indicating the Diameter credit-control application."
    range 4


;; DIAMETER_RATING_FAILED (5031), as sections 8.43 and 9.2 say too; which
;; AVPs the Failed-AVP holds is the server's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-rating-failed-failed-avp
; AVP: Failed-AVP
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 4.1.3
"A CCA message with this error MUST contain one or more Failed-AVP AVPs containing the missing and/or unsupported AVPs that caused the failure."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_RATING_FAILED


;; The session spans messages.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-session-id-the-sessions
; AVP: Session-Id
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.1
"Each credit-control session MUST have a globally unique Session-Id as defined in [DIAMBASE], which MUST NOT be changed during the lifetime of a credit-control session."
    text-only


;; Whether a tariff change occurred an earlier CCA's Tariff-Time-Change
;; says.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-used-service-unit-tariff-change
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.1.1
"When the Diameter credit-control client reports the used units and a tariff change has occurred during the reporting period, the Diameter credit-control client MUST separately itemize the units used before and after the tariff change."
    text-only


;; Which interrogation is the first, and what the client supports, the
;; request does not show.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-multiple-services-indicator-first-interrogation
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Indicator
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.1.2
"The credit-control client MUST indicate support for independent credit-control of multiple services within a (sub-)session by including the Multiple-Services-Indicator AVP in the first interrogation."
    text-only


;; The client's indication in an earlier request, the server's wish, and
;; two Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVPs compared.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-multiple-services-credit-control-granted-units
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 5.1.2
"If the client indicated support for independent credit-control of multiple services, a credit-control server that wishes to use the feature MUST return the granted units within the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP associated to the corresponding service-identifier and/or rating-group."
    text-only
"Both granted unit quotas MUST contain the same Service-Identifier and/or Rating-Group."
    text-only


;; Two AVPs' values compared, which no kind says.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: g-s-u-pool-reference-unit-types-differ
; AVP: G-S-U-Pool-Reference
; Within: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Section: 5.1.2
"Where multiple G-S-U-Pool-Reference AVPs (section 8.30) with the same G-S-U-Pool-Identifier are provided within a Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP (section 8.16) along with the Granted-Service-Unit AVP, then these MUST have different CC-Unit-Type values, and they all draw from the credit pool separately."
    text-only


;; The first interrogation is the CCR whose CC-Request-Type is
;; INITIAL_REQUEST; the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control's own scope does not
;; see it, so the rule is read on the CCR through a path into it, as section
;; 8.16 reads it too. Of several Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVPs, one
;; holding a Requested-Service-Unit meets the path.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-initial-multiple-services-credit-control-requested-units
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.2
"Where the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP is used, it MUST contain the Requested-Service-Unit AVP to indicate that the quota for the associated service/rating-group is requested."
    absent-if CC-Request-Type = INITIAL_REQUEST and not Multiple-Services-Credit-Control/Requested-Service-Unit


;; Which UPDATE_REQUEST is the first is the session's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-first-update-request-number
; AVP: CC-Request-Number
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.2.2
"The CC-Request-Number of the first UPDATE_REQUEST MUST be set to 1 (for how to produce unique value for the CC-Request-Number AVP, see section 8.2)."
    text-only


;; Whether the client requests a new quota, and which unit types the
;; previous answer held, the request does not show.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-update-multiple-services-credit-control-requested-units
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.3
"Where the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP is used, it MUST contain the Requested-Service-Unit AVP if a new quota is requested for the associated service/rating-group."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-update-used-service-unit-each-type
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.3
"If several unit types were included in the previous answer message, the used service units for each unit type MUST be reported."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-termination-used-service-unit-each-type
; AVP: Used-Service-Unit
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 5.4
"If several unit types were included in the previous answer message, the used service units for each unit type MUST be reported."
    text-only


;; The answer to the request an earlier CCA's final units ended.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-final-units-consumed-validity-time
; AVP: Validity-Time
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 5.6.2
"Naturally, the Credit-Control-Answer message does not contain any granted service unit and MUST include the Validity-Time AVP to indicate to the credit-control client how long the subscriber is allowed to use network resources before a new intermediate interrogation is sent to the server."
    text-only


;; Section 6's one-time events: the Requested-Action names the event, and
;; the CC-Request-Type, an Enumerated the values rule reads as its number,
;; is EVENT_REQUEST (4).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-price-enquiry-event-request
; AVP: CC-Request-Type
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.1
"A Diameter credit-control client requesting the cost information MUST set the CC-Request-Type AVP equal to EVENT_REQUEST, include the Requested-Action AVP set to PRICE_ENQUIRY, and set the requested service event information into the Service-Identifier AVP in the Credit-Control-Request message."
    values 4 if Requested-Action = PRICE_ENQUIRY


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-price-enquiry-service-identifier
; AVP: Service-Identifier
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.1
"A Diameter credit-control client requesting the cost information MUST set the CC-Request-Type AVP equal to EVENT_REQUEST, include the Requested-Action AVP set to PRICE_ENQUIRY, and set the requested service event information into the Service-Identifier AVP in the Credit-Control-Request message."
    present-if Requested-Action = PRICE_ENQUIRY


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-check-balance-event-request
; AVP: CC-Request-Type
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.2
"A Diameter credit-control client requesting the balance check MUST set the CC-Request-Type AVP equal to EVENT_REQUEST, include a Requested-Action AVP set to CHECK_BALANCE, and include the Subscription-Id AVP in order to identify the end user in the credit-control server."
    values 4 if Requested-Action = CHECK_BALANCE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-check-balance-subscription-id
; AVP: Subscription-Id
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.2
"A Diameter credit-control client requesting the balance check MUST set the CC-Request-Type AVP equal to EVENT_REQUEST, include a Requested-Action AVP set to CHECK_BALANCE, and include the Subscription-Id AVP in order to identify the end user in the credit-control server."
    present-if Requested-Action = CHECK_BALANCE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-refund-account-event-request
; AVP: CC-Request-Type
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 6.4
"The credit-control client MUST set CC-Request-Type to the value EVENT_REQUEST and the Requested-Action AVP to REFUND_ACCOUNT in the Credit-Control-Request message."
    values 4 if Requested-Action = REFUND_ACCOUNT


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-event-request-requested-action
; AVP: Requested-Action
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 8.3
"The Requested-Action AVP MUST be included in the Credit-Control-Request message when CC-Request-Type is set to EVENT_REQUEST."
    present-if CC-Request-Type = EVENT_REQUEST


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cc-session-failover-default
; AVP: CC-Session-Failover
; Section: 8.4
"FAILOVER_NOT_SUPPORTED 0 When the CC-Session-Failover AVP is set to FAILOVER_NOT_SUPPORTED, the credit-control message stream MUST NOT to be moved to an alternative destination in the case of communication failure."
"This is the default behavior if the AVP isn't included in the reply from the authorization or credit-control server."
    default FAILOVER_NOT_SUPPORTED


;; Earlier messages, and an absence meaning no value.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cc-sub-session-id-increasing
; AVP: CC-Sub-Session-Id
; Section: 8.5
"The combination of the Session-Id and this AVP MUST be unique per sub-session, and the value of this AVP MUST be monotonically increased by one for all new sub-sessions."
    text-only
"The absence of this AVP implies that no sub-sessions are in use."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: exponent-default
; AVP: Exponent
; Within: Unit-Value
; Section: 8.8
"The absence of the exponent part MUST be interpreted as an exponent equal to zero."
    default 0


;; ISO 4217's numeric codes, a document the corpus does not hold and no
;; element of the registry reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: currency-code-iso-4217
; AVP: Currency-Code
; Section: 8.11
"It is specified by using the numeric values defined in the ISO 4217 standard [ISO4217]."
    text-only


;; The service element's capabilities, and whether an AA request performs
;; the first interrogation or a re-authorization, are the node's and the
;; session's; the AA requests are other applications' commands.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: credit-control-in-aa-requests
; AVP: Credit-Control
; Section: 8.13
"The Credit-Control AVP (AVP Code 426) is of type Enumerated and MUST be included in AA requests when the service element has credit-control capabilities."
    text-only
"The value of the Credit-Control AVP MUST always be set to 0 in an AA request sent to perform the first interrogation and to initiate a new credit-control session."
    text-only
"This value MUST NOT be used in an AA request sent to perform the first interrogation."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: credit-control-failure-handling-default
; AVP: Credit-Control-Failure-Handling
; Section: 8.14
"This is the default behavior if the AVP isn't included in the reply from the authorization or credit-control server."
    default TERMINATE


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: direct-debiting-failure-handling-default
; AVP: Direct-Debiting-Failure-Handling
; Section: 8.15
"This is the default behavior if the AVP isn't included in the reply from the authorization server."
    default TERMINATE_OR_BUFFER


;; A pool's unit type names the member of the Granted-Service-Unit that
;; carries its units: TIME's CC-Time, MONEY's CC-Money, TOTAL-OCTETS',
;; INPUT-OCTETS' and OUTPUT-OCTETS' octet counts and SERVICE-SPECIFIC-UNITS'
;; CC-Service-Specific-Units (section 8.32). Of several
;; G-S-U-Pool-References, one of the type meets the path.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: g-s-u-pool-reference-granted-units
; AVP: G-S-U-Pool-Reference
; Within: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Section: 8.16
"If a G-S-U-Pool-Reference AVP is present, then actual service units of the specified type MUST also be present. For example, if the G-S-U-Pool-Reference AVP specifies Unit-Type TIME, then the CC-Time AVP MUST be present."
    excludes G-S-U-Pool-Reference/CC-Unit-Type = TIME and not Granted-Service-Unit/CC-Time or G-S-U-Pool-Reference/CC-Unit-Type = MONEY and not Granted-Service-Unit/CC-Money or G-S-U-Pool-Reference/CC-Unit-Type = TOTAL-OCTETS and not Granted-Service-Unit/CC-Total-Octets or G-S-U-Pool-Reference/CC-Unit-Type = INPUT-OCTETS and not Granted-Service-Unit/CC-Input-Octets or G-S-U-Pool-Reference/CC-Unit-Type = OUTPUT-OCTETS and not Granted-Service-Unit/CC-Output-Octets or G-S-U-Pool-Reference/CC-Unit-Type = SERVICE-SPECIFIC-UNITS and not Granted-Service-Unit/CC-Service-Specific-Units


;; The Requested-Service-Unit in the initial interrogation, as section 5.2
;; reads it; an intermediate interrogation's turns on whether the client
;; requests a new quota, and is not read. The request's Tariff-Change-Usage
;; is the Used-Service-Unit's member, not the Multiple-Services-Credit-
;; Control's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-multiple-services-credit-control-members
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 8.16
"It MUST be present in the initial interrogation and within the intermediate interrogations in which new quota is requested."
    absent-if CC-Request-Type = INITIAL_REQUEST and not Multiple-Services-Credit-Control/Requested-Service-Unit
"The Tariff-Change-Usage AVP MUST NOT be included in request commands to report used units before, and after tariff time change the Used-Service-Unit AVP MUST be used."
    absent-if Multiple-Services-Credit-Control/Tariff-Change-Usage


;; Two Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVPs, which no kind counts.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-tariff-change-two-quotas
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Credit-Control
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 8.16
"When both the Tariff-Time-Change and Tariff-Change-Usage AVPs are present, the server MUST include two separate instances of the Multiple-Services-Credit-Control AVP with the Granted-Service-Unit AVP associated to the same service-identifier and/or rating-group."
    text-only


;; An absence meaning no value.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tariff-time-change-omitted
; AVP: Tariff-Time-Change
; Section: 8.20
"Omission of this AVP means that no tariff change is to be reported."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tariff-change-usage-omitted
; AVP: Tariff-Change-Usage
; Section: 8.27
"Omission of this AVP means that no tariff change has occurred."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: final-unit-indication-terminate
; AVP: Final-Unit-Indication
; Section: 8.34
"If the Final-Unit-Action AVP is set to TERMINATE, no other AVPs MUST be present."
    excludes Final-Unit-Action = TERMINATE and Restriction-Filter-Rule or Final-Unit-Action = TERMINATE and Filter-Id or Final-Unit-Action = TERMINATE and Redirect-Server


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: final-unit-indication-redirect-server
; AVP: Redirect-Server
; Within: Final-Unit-Indication
; Section: 8.34
"If the Final-Unit-Action AVP is set to REDIRECT at least the Redirect-Server AVP MUST be present."
    present-if Final-Unit-Action = REDIRECT


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: redirect-server-redirect
; AVP: Redirect-Server
; Within: Final-Unit-Indication
; Section: 8.37
"It MUST be present when the Final-Unit-Action AVP is set to REDIRECT."
    present-if Final-Unit-Action = REDIRECT


;; A text's form chosen by a sibling's value, which no kind reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: redirect-server-address-by-type
; AVP: Redirect-Server-Address
; Within: Redirect-Server
; Section: 8.38
"IPv4 Address 0 The address type is in the form of \"dotted-decimal\" IPv4 address, as defined in [IPv4]."
"IPv6 Address 1 The address type is in the form of IPv6 address, as defined in [IPv6Addr]. The address is a text representation of the address in either the preferred or alternate text form [IPv6Addr]."
"URL 2 The address type is in the form of Uniform Resource Locator, as defined in [URL]."
"SIP URI 3 The address type is in the form of SIP Uniform Resource Identifier, as defined in [SIP]."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: multiple-services-indicator-default
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Indicator
; Section: 8.40
"The absence of this AVP means that independent credit-control of multiple services is not supported."
    default MULTIPLE_SERVICES_NOT_SUPPORTED


;; Who allocates the identifier, and a text's form, which no codec reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: service-context-id-format
; AVP: Service-Context-Id
; Section: 8.42
"This is an identifier allocated by the service provider, by the service element manufacturer, or by a standardization body, and MUST uniquely identify a given Diameter credit-control service specific document."
    text-only
"\"service-context\" \"@\" \"domain\""
    text-only


;; As section 4.1.3's; which Service-Parameter-Info caused the failure is
;; the server's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-unknown-service-failed-avp
; AVP: Failed-AVP
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 8.43
"A Credit-Control-Answer message with this error MUST contain one or more Failed-AVP AVPs containing the Service-Parameter-Info AVPs that caused the failure."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_RATING_FAILED


;; A text's form chosen by a sibling's value, which no kind reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: subscription-id-data-by-type
; AVP: Subscription-Id-Data
; Within: Subscription-Id
; Section: 8.47
"END_USER_E164 0 The identifier is in international E.164 format (e.g., MSISDN), according to the ITU-T E.164 numbering plan defined in [E164] and [CE164]."
"END_USER_IMSI 1 The identifier is in international IMSI format, according to the ITU-T E.212 numbering plan as defined in [E212] and [CE212]."
"END_USER_SIP_URI 2 The identifier is in the form of a SIP URI, as defined in [SIP]."
"END_USER_NAI 3 The identifier is in the form of a Network Access Identifier, as defined in [NAI]."
    text-only


;; Octets chosen by a sibling's value, which no kind reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: user-equipment-info-value-by-type
; AVP: User-Equipment-Info-Value
; Within: User-Equipment-Info
; Section: 8.50
"IMEISV 0 The identifier contains the International Mobile Equipment Identifier and Software Version in the international IMEISV format according to 3GPP TS 23.003 [3GPPIMEI]."
"MAC 1 The 48-bit MAC address is formatted as described in [RAD802.1X]."
"EUI64 2 The 64-bit identifier used to identify hardware instance of the product, as defined in [EUI64]."
    text-only


;; As section 4.1.3's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-rating-failed-result-failed-avp
; AVP: Failed-AVP
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 9.2
"The Failed-AVP AVP MUST be included and contain a copy of the entire AVP(s) that could not be processed successfully or an example of the missing AVP complete with the Vendor-Id if applicable."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_RATING_FAILED


;; Table 10.1's CCR column: what its "0" says the Credit-Control-Request
;; never carries, an AVP its body admits only through * [ AVP ].
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-cc-session-failover-table-absent
; AVP: CC-Session-Failover
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"CC-Session-Failover | 0 | 0-1 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-check-balance-result-table-absent
; AVP: Check-Balance-Result
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Check-Balance-Result | 0 | 0-1 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-cost-information-table-absent
; AVP: Cost-Information
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Cost-Information | 0 | 0-1 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-credit-control-failure-handling-table-absent
; AVP: Credit-Control-Failure-Handling
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Credit-Control-Failure- | 0 | 0-1 | Handling | | |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-direct-debiting-failure-handling-table-absent
; AVP: Direct-Debiting-Failure-Handling
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Direct-Debiting-Failure- | 0 | 0-1 | Handling | | |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-failed-avp-table-absent
; AVP: Failed-AVP
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Failed-AVP | 0 | 0+ |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-final-unit-indication-table-absent
; AVP: Final-Unit-Indication
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Final-Unit-Indication | 0 | 0-1 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-granted-service-unit-table-absent
; AVP: Granted-Service-Unit
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Granted-Service-Unit | 0 | 0-1 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-redirect-host-table-absent
; AVP: Redirect-Host
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Redirect-Host | 0 | 0+ |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-redirect-host-usage-table-absent
; AVP: Redirect-Host-Usage
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Redirect-Host-Usage | 0 | 0-1 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-redirect-max-cache-time-table-absent
; AVP: Redirect-Max-Cache-Time
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Redirect-Max-Cache-Time | 0 | 0-1 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-result-code-table-absent
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Result-Code | 0 | 1 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: ccr-validity-time-table-absent
; AVP: Validity-Time
; Command: Credit-Control-Request
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Validity-Time | 0 | 0-1 |"
    absent


;; Table 10.1's CCA column: what its "0" says the Credit-Control-Answer
;; never carries, an AVP its body admits only through * [ AVP ].
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-cc-correlation-id-table-absent
; AVP: CC-Correlation-Id
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"CC-Correlation-Id | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-destination-host-table-absent
; AVP: Destination-Host
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Destination-Host | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-destination-realm-table-absent
; AVP: Destination-Realm
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Destination-Realm | 1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-multiple-services-indicator-table-absent
; AVP: Multiple-Services-Indicator
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Multiple-Services-Indicator | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-requested-action-table-absent
; AVP: Requested-Action
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Requested-Action | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-requested-service-unit-table-absent
; AVP: Requested-Service-Unit
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Requested-Service-Unit | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-service-context-id-table-absent
; AVP: Service-Context-Id
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Service-Context-Id | 1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-service-identifier-table-absent
; AVP: Service-Identifier
; Command: Credit-Control-Answer
; Section: 10.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message."
"Service-Identifier | 0-1 | 0 |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: cca-service-parameter-info-table-absent
; AVP: Service-Parameter-Info
